From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: PS5: exclude unmappable host addresses from free queries

Wine measures host_addr_space_limit and rejects fixed allocations past it.
Its memory query nevertheless advertises the same range as MEM_FREE. An emulator's
scan then attempts an allocation that Wine already knows cannot succeed.

Keep Windows views authoritative, bound ordinary free gaps by the existing
measured limit, and describe the unavailable upper range as reserved, using
Wine's existing fake_reserved query representation. No address constants,
synthetic allocation success, relocation, or host configuration changes.

SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -6547,7 +6547,19 @@
 #ifdef __PROSPERO__
     {
         void *start, *end;
-        int status = pw_wine_vm_gap( base, *region_end, query_wine_reserved_area, &start, &end );
+        int status;
+
+        /* Fixed allocations already reject this range. Do not advertise it
+         * as free to Windows address-space scanners. Existing views above
+         * the measured host limit were handled by the tree lookup first. */
+        if (base >= (char *)host_addr_space_limit)
+        {
+            *region_start = max( *region_start, (char *)host_addr_space_limit );
+            *fake_reserved = TRUE;
+            return NULL;
+        }
+        *region_end = min( *region_end, (char *)host_addr_space_limit );
+        status = pw_wine_vm_gap( base, *region_end, query_wine_reserved_area, &start, &end );
 
         if (status < 0) WARN( "cannot query native mapping at %p\n", base );
         else
